# `Function` and `BiFunction`

## `java.util.function` — ready-made shapes

Don't declare your own — target the standard interfaces.

## `Function<T, R>` — transform: `apply`

```java
Function<String, Integer> length = s -> s.length();
length.apply("hello");   // 5   —  T in, R out
```

## `BiFunction<T, U, R>` — two inputs

```java
BiFunction<Integer, Integer, Integer> add = (a, b) -> a + b;
```

No `TriFunction` — need three? pass a record.

## Same-type aliases

- **`UnaryOperator<T>`** = `Function<T,T>` — `list.replaceAll(...)`
- **`BinaryOperator<T>`** = `BiFunction<T,T,T>` — `stream.reduce(...)`

## Primitive variants (no boxing)

`IntFunction` (takes int) · `ToIntFunction` (returns int) · `IntUnaryOperator` (int→int)
